    "lium_min_executors": 2,
    "lium_note": "`lium_tier` is the on-demand product; `lium_accelerators` is the substring set that defines 'comparable tier'. Both are declared here rather than hard-coded in scripts/anchors.py so a reader can see what was included without reading the fetcher.",
    "lium_thin_note": "A class priced off fewer than `lium_min_executors` secure executors is marked `quality.thin` in the anchor and counted in `provenance.n_accelerator_classes_thin`; `lium_max_thin` is how many of the six classes may be thin before `--check` fails. A median over one executor is that executor's ASK, and SN51 inventory is ~93% idle, so this is a real and recurring condition rather than an outage: `NVIDIA H200 NVL` was already at n=1 in the 2026-10-29 anchor, and `NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3` went 6 to 1 inside 24h on 2026-10-30. The thin row is still PRICED on purpose -- dropping it would put the basket under `min_priced` above, which flips `par.Basket.usable` and reprices an outsider's bill onto the fleet's own quotes, 10x to 1250x off market by anchors/GAP.md. One disclosed thin row inside a ten-row median is a far smaller error than that. Ceiling set at 2 (measured 1 at the 2026-10-29 anchor, 2 live the next day); lower it deliberately in a commit.",
    "lium_tier": "secure",
    "min_priced": 10,
    "min_priced_note": "How many rows must actually carry a price. A ratchet, like the anchor's own `ceiling`: the basket has thinned before, ACR-INF going from 6 to 5 priced of 10 requested with no signal anywhere, and `par.Basket.usable` sends a stranger's bill to the FLEET scale once a basket stops being usable \u2014 a scale anchors/GAP.md puts 10x to 1250x off market. Lower it deliberately in a commit, or fix the fetch. Raised 4 \u2192 10 on 2026-10-29, in the same change as the fetch that first priced the six Lium accelerator classes: a floor left at 4 would have let the Bittensor rows vanish silently and re-medianed the four rate cards as if nothing had changed.",
    "note": "Median across providers for a comparable accelerator tier.",
    "trim": 0.0,
    "unit_conversion": "usd_per_gpu_hour / 3600"
  },
